# LXP Protocol and Inverter Communication

## Protocol Structure
The LXP protocol implementation is in [src/lxp/mod.rs](mdc:src/lxp/mod.rs) and includes:
- **Packet Handling**: [src/lxp/packet.rs](mdc:src/lxp/packet.rs) - Binary packet encoding/decoding
- **Packet Decoding**: [src/lxp/packet_decoder.rs](mdc:src/lxp/packet_decoder.rs) - Protocol parsing
- **Inverter Interface**: [src/lxp/inverter.rs](mdc:src/lxp/inverter.rs) - High-level inverter operations

## Packet Architecture
- Use `Packet` and `PacketCommon` traits for protocol operations
- Implement proper CRC16 validation for packet integrity
- Handle TCP and UDP packet types appropriately
- Use `nom` for binary protocol parsing

## Inverter Operations
- Implement async communication patterns
- Handle connection management and reconnection
- Use proper error handling for network failures
- Implement timeout handling for operations

## Register Operations
- Support both holding registers and input registers
- Implement proper register address mapping
- Handle register value validation and conversion
- Support bit-level operations where needed

## Register Documentation
**CRITICAL**: Always reference these documentation files for inverter communication:
- **[doc/MODBUS_PROTOCOL.md](mdc:doc/MODBUS_PROTOCOL.md)** - Complete Modbus RTU protocol specification
- **[doc/HOLD_REGISTERS.md](mdc:doc/HOLD_REGISTERS.md)** - All read/write hold registers (0x03, 0x06, 0x10)
- **[doc/INPUT_REGISTERS.md](mdc:doc/INPUT_REGISTERS.md)** - All read-only input registers (0x04)
- **[doc/REGISTER_MAPPING.md](mdc:doc/REGISTER_MAPPING.md)** - Overview and quick reference guide

## Protocol Compliance
- Follow the Modbus protocol specifications in [doc/MODBUS_PROTOCOL.md](mdc:doc/MODBUS_PROTOCOL.md)
- Implement proper function codes for different operations
- Handle device addressing and serial numbers
- Support both read and write operations
- **IMPORTANT**: Maximum 40 registers per query, must align with group boundaries (0, 40, 80, 120, etc.)
